The tick ends a share's turn without putting the share back on the run queue.
A share with another ready thread would leave it behind for good;
every share with a ready thread but the one whose turn it is waits on the run queue.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a share with a ready thread waits on no queue

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -536,9 +536,7 @@ static void turn_end(void)
 {
     struct share *was = turn;
     turn = NULL;
-    if (was != NULL) {
-        share_settle(was);
-    }
+    (void)was;
     enqueue(current);
     turn = next_turn();
     run_turn();
